{"id": "EUVD-2026-93221", "enisaUuid": "534cd7ae-ee5e-303b-be61-359aac0c37c4", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: ISO: Fix parent socket leak in iso_conn_ready()\n\niso_get_sock() returns the parent socket with a reference held, which is\ndropped by sock_put() once the child socket has been set up. The error\npath taken when iso_sock_alloc() fails only calls release_sock() and\nreturns, leaking the reference and thus the parent socket itself.\n\nDrop the reference on that path as well.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:45:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:17:04", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ea8a262662be62c095789924c11722ecbf40a4de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9228f87365e68a6cae191f57f456e89a6d2167cf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2b156a8d25966be49c1f809b654a2c4bb16564d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f016daabd4fec4e9b8563f8b6f42eabce0ca66b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca18ee413a7cb6f09885778039225e58bae0d607"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m9gh-q95c-rcfx", "CVE-2026-98293"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "292e8b8d-fd6c-3223-b9c4-668359a0bac0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3465baef-e18f-3b26-89c5-b59eb4f1046a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fa224d0c094a458e9ebf5ea9b1c696136b7af427 <e2b156a8d25966be49c1f809b654a2c4bb16564d"}, {"id": "536566c5-c7d9-35a2-b87c-e155d57a9f94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "5c078a6f-4c24-3c29-8a2b-424549880d75", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fa224d0c094a458e9ebf5ea9b1c696136b7af427 <ca18ee413a7cb6f09885778039225e58bae0d607"}, {"id": "8e65002e-12fb-3bf4-9947-6cfe32911dd9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54